Description: Skip /usr/include in test include paths to fix #include_next
 When OpenCL_INCLUDE_DIR or UR_OPENCL_INCLUDE_DIR is set to /usr/include,
 adding it as an -isystem path breaks #include_next in libstdc++ headers.
 The cstdlib header uses #include_next to find the C library's stdlib.h,
 which requires /usr/include to appear AFTER the C++ headers in the search
 path. Explicitly adding it with -isystem moves it to the front, breaking
 this mechanism. Since /usr/include is already in clang's default search
 path in the correct position, we simply skip it when building test flags.
Author: Will French <will.french@canonical.com>
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-01-09
---
--- a/sycl/test/lit.cfg.py	2026-01-09 10:12:08.278081602 -0600
+++ b/sycl/test/lit.cfg.py	2026-01-09 10:12:16.898712452 -0600
@@ -128,7 +128,8 @@
     config.opencl_include_dir,
     config.sycl_include + "/sycl/",
 ]:
-    if include_dir:
+    # Skip /usr/include to avoid breaking #include_next in libstdc++ headers
+    if include_dir and include_dir != "/usr/include/" and include_dir != "/usr/include":
         sycl_host_only_options += " -isystem %s" % include_dir
 config.substitutions.append(("%fsycl-host-only", sycl_host_only_options))
 
